Catch file IO errors without intercepting the receive deadline or thread
cancellation. The server wraps receiveFile in timeout; catching SomeException
inside it turned its timeout into FILE_IO and swallowed ThreadKilled too.
HTTP2Error still maps to TIMEOUT, and IOException still maps to FILE_IO.

Index: src/Simplex/FileTransfer/Transport.hs
--- src/Simplex/FileTransfer/Transport.hs.orig
+++ src/Simplex/FileTransfer/Transport.hs
@@ -177,7 +177,9 @@ receiveFile getBody chunk = ExceptT $ ru
     receive h sz = hReceiveFile getBody h sz >>= \sz' -> pure $ if sz' == 0 then Right () else Left SIZE
     handlers =
       [ E.Handler $ \(e :: HTTP2Error) -> logWarn (err e) $> Left TIMEOUT,
-        E.Handler $ \(e :: E.SomeException) -> logError (err e) $> Left FILE_IO
+        -- Let timeout and cancellation reach their owners. Catching
+        -- SomeException here turns the server's receive timeout into FILE_IO.
+        E.Handler $ \(e :: E.IOException) -> logError (err e) $> Left FILE_IO
       ]
     err e = "receiveFile error: " <> tshow e
 
